* text=auto eol=lf

*.blade.php diff=html
*.css diff=css
*.html diff=html
*.md diff=markdown
*.php diff=php

CHANGELOG.md export-ignore
/README.md export-ignore

# These describe the KIT itself, so they must not ship into scaffolded projects — a project born
# asserting "PR target repo: artisan-build/built-for-cloud-starter" sends agents at the wrong repository.
# App-facing replacements live in stubs/ and are installed by post-create-project-cmd. Anchored with a
# leading slash so stubs/CLAUDE.md is NOT caught by this rule.
/CLAUDE.md export-ignore
/.solo export-ignore
/composer.lock export-ignore

# Same rule, applied to a workflow rather than docs. This one asserts things about the REPOSITORY it
# lives in — that "Allow auto-merge" is on and that `main` has required status checks — and both are
# false in a freshly scaffolded project. GitHub only offers auto-merge on a PR that cannot merge
# immediately, so in a repo without required checks there is nothing to wait for and the workflow
# would merge dependency updates with no CI gate at all. Auto-merge should be opted into by someone
# who has also done the branch-protection work that makes it safe; README.md says how.
#
# .github/dependabot.yml is deliberately NOT listed here — it stays true in any Laravel repo, so
# scaffolded projects get dependency updates for free and can delete the file if they'd rather not.
/.github/workflows/dependabot-auto-merge.yml export-ignore

# These exercise kit-only source state (stubs, Git metadata, and the export-ignored kit documents).
# The generated app keeps the remaining application tests as its starter suite.
/tests/Unit/BuiltForCloudSkillsTest.php export-ignore
/tests/Unit/InstallStubsTest.php export-ignore
/tests/Unit/StarterConventionsTest.php export-ignore
